        "text": "# Project Helios\nKB page ID: 9d08f9fb-ac64-4094-a3e1-24c25bc01480\nPath: Project Helios (root)\nType: project | Rev: 1 | Created: 2026-10-14 | Updated: 2026-10-14 | Sources: 7 | Wiki: Synthetic KB 003085a3 (project id 2c5cd7a8-2225-4170-b71d-b49fd1bb4b9b)\nChildren: Decision: Helios Lead Selection, Helios HX-01 Thermal Stability Screen, Helios HX-02 Buffer Blocking Optimization, Helios HX-03 Signal Artifact Characterization, Helios HX-04 Dose Response in Primary Cells, Helios HX-05 Scale-up Feasibility (Draft), Helios Q2 2024 Review\nLinked from (3 pages, by type):\n  person (2): Dana Whitfield, Maja Lindqvist\n  organization (1): Northwind Biosciences\nLinks to: Dana Whitfield\n\n<!-- sec:sec_charter -->\n## Charter\n\nThe program exists to find a thermostable lead from the NW-200 scaffold series for oral delivery (helios-program-charter.pdf › block 1). It is headed by [[Dana Whitfield]] (helios-program-charter.pdf › block 2).\n\n<!-- sec:sec_budget -->\n## Budget\n\nFiscal 2024 funding is USD 2.4 million, reviewed each quarter by the portfolio committee (helios-program-charter.pdf › block 3).\n\n<!-- sec:sec_success_criterion -->\n## Success criterion\n\nA lead must keep at least 80 percent of its activity after two weeks at 40 degrees Celsius (helios-program-charter.pdf › block 4).\n\n<!-- sec:sec_lead_decision -->\n## Lead decision  [2024-09-09]\n\nThe portfolio committee approved NW-217 as the lead on 9 September 2024 (helios-go-decision-memo.docx › block 1).\n\nSection date metadata:\n- sec_lead_decision (Lead decision): event_start=2024-09-09; date_precision=day\n\n---\nSources cited above:\n  - [artifact:upload:synthetic_kb] helios-go-decision-memo.docx\n  - [artifact:upload:synthetic_kb] helios-program-charter.pdf\n\nNote: This page is an AI-compiled summary, and the documents above are the ones its text cites. Each citation in the body names its document and the place in it (memo.pdf › p. 7), which read_file opens. Excerpts, the section(s) each source supports or contradicts, and this page's other 5 source record(s) are NOT shown here -- run `sources Project Helios` or `provenance Project Helios` for those. Open the original before quoting or before resting a conclusion on it.",
